---
description: Issue-to-PR workflow and hard limits for Cursor sessions
alwaysApply: true
---
Cursor has no pre-commit or pre-PR hook in this repository, so follow these steps yourself.

1. Work only on one GitHub issue that is labelled `ready`. Claim it: assign yourself, add `in-progress`, comment "Working on this."
2. Work in a separate git worktree on a branch `feat/<issue#>-<slug>` (or `fix/`, `docs/`, `chore/`) cut from up-to-date `origin/main`: `git worktree add ../wt-<issue#> -b <branch> origin/main`. Never commit to `main` and never switch the branch of the main checkout.
3. Write the failing test first. Never weaken or delete a test to make it pass.
4. Before every commit run all four, and fix failures instead of skipping them: `npm test`, `npm run test:e2e`, `npm run lint`, `npm run format:check`.
5. Open a pull request whose body contains `Closes #<issue#>`. Comment the PR link on the issue.

Keeping a branch mergeable (same rules as `AGENTS.md`):
- Before starting work, and again before opening or updating a pull request, merge `origin/main` into the branch: `git fetch origin && git merge origin/main`. Merge; never rebase and never force-push.
- Before reporting a task done, run `gh pr view <number> --json mergeable,mergeStateStatus` and wait for the checks of the newest commit (`gh pr checks <number> --watch`), not an older run.
- The report states the mergeable status and the check result.
- If a merge conflict touches a file whose behaviour both sides changed, stop and report the conflict instead of choosing a side.

Hard limits:
- Never merge a pull request, never push to `main`, never run deploy commands (`vercel`, production deploys).
- Never read, print or paste `.env*` files, `secrets/`, or any key value. Real values live only in the local `.env` and in Vercel environment settings.
- Never put the Supabase service-role key or any model API key in app code or in a `NEXT_PUBLIC_` variable.
- Changes to colors, spacing or controls must follow `DESIGN.md`.
- Do not edit `.claude/`, `AGENTS.md` or rule files unless the issue asks for it.
